      "writtenOn": "2026-03-25T17:30:49Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I think I found the issue with `powerindebug`.  The [`power_signal_gpio_get()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/signal_gpio.c;l\u003d112;drc\u003d428663122197837fe3a3691dfe30cdef4d0bd1e7) routine doesn\u0027t read the input register for GPIOs configured as an output.\n\nBernardo - should the linked code check whether the signal is configured for open drain or push-pull?  For push-pull is should be valid to always call `gpio_pin_get_dt()`",
      "parentUuid": "03b8af7c_62160dcd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "f8ad521f017be0b09c5f688297be503f39a34cb5",
